explanation:
Diamond problem: without virtual inheritance, D contains duplicate A. Ambiguity: which A's methods to call? <br>
Solutions: <br>
(1) virtual inheritance (single A), (2) use explicit path (B::method_from_A()), (3) redesign hierarchy (composition instead of multiple inheritance). Virtual inheritance: class B : virtual public A; class C : virtual public A;

